## Why This Is Asked
To evaluate design of a real-time, privacy-preserving NLP system handling 40 languages with strict per-tenant isolation, enforceable retention, and robust rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time streaming NLP in a multi-tenant setting
- Multilingual PII/financial data detection
- In-flight redaction and per-tenant policy routing
- Edge vs cloud processing trade-offs
- Privacy-preserving data handling and auditing
- Rollback, versioning, and test strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code sketch: detect and redact PII in a streaming row
function processRow(row, tenantPolicy){
  const entities = piiModel.detect(row.text, tenantPolicy.languages);
  const redacted = redact(entities, row.text);
  logAudit(row.id, tenantPolicy.id, entities);
  return redacted;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure privacy leakage risk in production?
- How would you keep model updates per-tenant isolated during rollout?

## Why This Is Asked

Probes on-device NLP, privacy, and latency trade-offs in edge deployments typical of Cloudflare/Uber-scale products.

## Key Concepts

- On-device inference with deterministic latency
- Regex-based redaction plus tiny ML for edge cases
- Multilingual and code-switching handling
- Privacy controls and local data labeling

## Code Example

```javascript
const redact = (text) => {
  const emails = /[\w.+-]+@[\w.-]+\.[a-zA-Z]{2,}/g;
  const phones = /(\+?\d[\d\s\-\(\)]{7,}\d)/g;
  let out = text.replace(emails, "[REDACTED_EMAIL]");
  out = out.replace(phones, "[REDACTED_PHONE]");
  out = out.replace(/\b[A-Z][a-z]+ [A-Z][a-z]+\b/g, "[REDACTED_NAME]");
  return out;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure and guarantee 100 ms latency across devices?
- How would you handle false positives and user-triggered corrections without server contact?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a practical, multilingual, on-device NLP component with concrete constraints and a simple evaluation path.

## Key Concepts
- Lightweight NER: lexicon + rules, tiny ML fallback
- Multilingual tokenization: EN/ES/DE handling
- Taxonomy normalization and confidence scoring
- On-device privacy and rollout strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
function extractMentions(text, lexicon) {
  const mentions = [];
  for (const [word, label] of Object.entries(lexicon)) {
    if (text.includes(word)) mentions.push({ word, label });
  }
  return mentions;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle ambiguous mentions across languages?
- What metrics and thresholds would you use for the confidence score, and how would you validate them on-device?

## Why This Question Is Asked

This question evaluates system design proficiency for cross-language NLP with strict privacy and real-time performance constraints. It also tests understanding of knowledge graph integration and disaster recovery mechanisms.

## Key Concepts

- **Streaming multilingual NER**: Continuous entity extraction across 25 languages in real-time
- **Cross-language alias resolution**: Linking entities across different languages to a canonical form
- **Privacy-preserving per-tenant embeddings**: Isolated embedding spaces that prevent data leakage between tenants
- **Edge-friendly inference**: Lightweight models deployable close to data sources for minimal latency
- **Knowledge graph drift and rollback**: Tracking schema/behavior changes with the ability to revert safely

## Architecture Overview

```javascript
// Streaming pipeline architecture
async function processIncidentReport(text, tenant, metadata) {
  const normalized = await normalize(text);
  const entities = await runMultilingualNER(normalized, tenant);
  const linked = await resolveCrossLingualAliases(entities, sharedIndex);
  await updateKnowledgeGraph(linked, tenant, metadata);
  return { entities, aliases, confidence };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you evaluate cross-language alias accuracy across diverse language pairs?
- What rollback strategies would you implement for knowledge graph inconsistencies?
- How would you detect and handle model drift in production?
- What privacy guarantees do per-tenant embeddings provide against inference attacks?

